 "about_text": "KOTARO NUKAGA is a contemporary art gallery founded in Tokyo in 2018 by director Kotaro Nukaga, who also runs the historic NUKAGA GALLERY. The gallery operates three spaces in Tokyo—two in the Tennoz district (Tennoz and Three) and one in Roppongi—positioning itself at the intersection of Japanese and international contemporary practice. Its program favors avant-garde and cross-disciplinary work, drawing on history, science and technology to question established art-world discourse. The gallery represents a mix of emerging and established Japanese and overseas artists, supporting their development through exhibitions, artist liaison services and participation in international art fairs, while aiming to expand the boundaries of conventional gallery programming.",
